   "provider": "Wikimedia Commons",
   "title": "City Opera House, Traverse City, MI.jpg",
   "description": "The City Opera House in Traverse City is a significant building on Front Street in the city's downtown, constructed in 1891 in the Romanesque Revival style, and contained a 1200 seat auditorium for live performances. In the 1920s, a nearby movie theatre owner leased the building in order to eliminate the possibility of it becoming competition for their own theater, and it remained shuttered and largely unused until 1985, when, thanks to the efforts of the local community and preservationists, it reopened as a live performance venue, with renovations finally completed in 2005. Today, the restored building is one of the most notable historic landmarks in Traverse City, and is one of the city's many historic assets.",
   "creator": "w_lemay",
   "licence": "CC0",
